WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.660
Let the Battinson bonanza begin.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:06.820
When Matt Reeves, the co-writer and director
of the upcoming superhero film The Batman,

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:11.080
shared to Twitter the first camera test of
Robert Pattinson as Gotham's greatest protector,

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.260
the internet practically collapsed in on itself.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.230
For a brief moment, it felt as though the
world stopped turning, a sudden halt spurred

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:20.500
by the thousands of tweets sent out by fans
responding to the big reveal.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.060
"Time is a thing that grows scarcer everyday.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.440
What, you don't know this?"

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.560
As with any reveal of this sort, one that
gives the world the first official glimpse

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:33.780
of an actor in costume as a beloved, internationally
recognized pop culture figure, reactions to

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.640
Pattinson as Batman have been mixed.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.940
The majority of early responses to the reveal
were positive, with countless Twitter users

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:41.660
gushing over the first-look footage.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:42.720
One user wrote,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:43.760
"I'm ecstatic.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.200
This movie will be amazing."

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:49.440
Another added that they enjoyed both the way
the Battinson suit looks and the score teased

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.160
in the camera test video, writing,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.179
"The Batman teaser looked really dope.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.740
I especially loved the tone that was playing
during it.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.020
Hope to get a fleshed out version of it when
it releases."

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.900
Plenty of fans analyzed the video with a keener
eye, picking up on possible references to

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.520
Batman's past and to other iterations of the
character.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:10.120
Comparisons were made between the new Batsuit
for The Batman and the costumes seen in Batman:

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:13.360
Arkham Knight, Arkham Origins, and Batman:
Gotham Knight.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:17.980
Many also noted that the video felt somewhat
like a tease for a Daredevil project, since

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:22.100
it's dimly lit and doused in a striking red
hue similar to the color of the Marvel hero's

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:22.660
suit.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.740
One Twitter user wrote,

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.420
"I'm definitely getting some Daredevil vibes.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.980
The new Batman suit looks incredible for what
it is.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.540
Man I'm so excited for Matt Reeves take on
the character."

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:36.560
One fan, who was actually one of several who
presented this theory, posited that the new

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.050
Bat-symbol could be made from a gun, perhaps
the one used to murder Bruce Wayne's parents.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.380
That fan also wrote on Twitter that Pattinson
"looks amazing," and that they "can't wait"

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.220
to see The Batman.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:47.760
Another fan tweeted,

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.060
"A simple camera test and I am 300 times more
excited for Pattinson as Batman."

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:56.860
The initial wave of positive reactions to
the Battinson reveal was soon met with a negative

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:57.840
wave, naturally.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:02.640
Some people slammed the reveal video as "lame"
and "stupid," and used plenty of unsavory

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:05.480
words to criticize the way Pattinson looks
as Batman.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:06.940
One use tweeted,

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:11.420
"So basically it's yet another ugly armor
suit, only this time they couldn't even be

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:13.180
bothered to make the emblem look good.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:13.880
Wow.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.800
Is there a rule at WB/DC that no Batman actor
can have a decent-looking costume anymore?"

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:23.460
"These questions are vital ones."

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.060
Another fan wrote on Twitter,

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.599
"The new Batman suit is ugly if you ask me.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.680
I do like the mask and the collar, but I'm
not a fan of the armor look."

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:35.880
Meanwhile, NRG Esports' Richard "KingRichard"
Nelson didn't mince his words, writing,

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.300
"Bruh that Batman reveal is terrible."

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.560
This trend of unfiltered reactions to the
reveal continued all across Twitter, with

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:43.660
one fan tweeting,

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.930
"Excuse me for my language but that is just
f---ing awful!

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:50.890
I know [Ben] Affleck had doubters, but as
soon as we saw him in the suit, no one, no

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:51.900
one doubted then!

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.600
I'm a huge batman fan and this may very well
be the first time I don't go see the movie."

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.960
While that fan clearly believes Ben Affleck
was the best Batman and that Pattinson can

00:03:00.969 --> 00:03:05.019
never measure up, others have said that seeing
this reveal for The Batman solidifies the

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:08.360
notion that Christian Bale is the best actor
to have stepped into the Batsuit.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:09.720
One user argued,

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.060
"Batman should have ended when Christian bale
stopped playing him.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.209
Stop over killing it!

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:17.820
Affleck was terrible, Robert is out here looking
like daredevil...STOP IT."

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:23.460
All things considered, this feels like a fairly
normal response to a reveal of this caliber.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.519
Some fans have maintained a cool head and
advised others do the same until The Batman

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.780
actually opens in theaters.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.260
As one fan tweeted,

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.859
"People deciding the new Batman is s--- after
one short teaser image...I thought Guardians

00:03:34.859 --> 00:03:37.029
of the Galaxy looked terrible after one image.

00:03:37.029 --> 00:03:38.540
A talking raccoon and a tree?

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:39.040
No, thanks.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.680
Yeah, it's one of my favourite films.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:42.240
Wait and see."

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:46.300
The Batman flies into theaters on June 25,
2021.

